  "body": "Probably the number 1 and most notable issue we receive as feedback from the community.\r\n\r\nThe [upgrade page in the docs site](https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/develop/upgrading/index.html) ([source](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a0cd8ae8cbe14d2821cbe8fd6b011c4ddc729344/docs/upgrading/README.md)) is currently generated from [UPGRADE.rst](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a0cd8ae8cbe14d2821cbe8fd6b011c4ddc729344/UPGRADE.rst) in the root of the repository.\r\n\r\nmdbook expects markdown instead of RST, and thus the page looks a bit broken. We could convert UPGRADE.rst to a markdown file, though that would break existing links to the file (and this file is linked to quite frequently).\r\n\r\nPossible solutions I can think of:\r\n\r\n1. Don't import UPGRADE.rst into a mdbook page and instead simply link to the page on GitHub. This is probably the easiest solution.\r\n1. Convert UPGRADE.rst to docs/UPGRADE.md, and leave UPGRADE.rst in place with a link to the docs website. Also quite a simple solution, although anyone who's linked to a specific header on UPGRADE.rst will have a bad time.\r\n1. Use a [mdbook preprocessor](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/format/configuration/preprocessors.html) to convert RST to markdown while building the book.\r\n    * Preprocessors can essentially modify the contents of a page during book rendering. I haven't seen one for RST -> MD yet though.\r\n\r\nThoughts?",
